        "feedback": {
          "grade": "Correct",
          "source_grade": "Correct",
          "result": "Correct",
          "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=15$ into the expression for $p(x)$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a{x}^{2}+bx \\\\ p(15) & =a(15)^{2}+b(15) \\\\  & =225a+15b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p(15)=225a+15b.$",
          "solution_evidence": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245623/observations/history-solution-q-167216-5d8ff2e21264e5c1aa93.html",
          "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245623/observations/history-q-167216-41d0e1e0a5d9302d7d3c.html"
        }
      },
      {
        "question_id": "q-167217",
        "problem": "If the company produces fifteen wooden tables in a week, the weekly profit will be $$4\\,050.$ Find an expression for $b$ in terms of $a.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $b=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "answers": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
            "correct_value": "270-15a",
            "ma_basis": "none"
          }
        ],
        "feedback": {
          "grade": "Correct",
          "source_grade": "Correct",
          "result": "Correct",
          "worked_solution": "In part 1, we found that $p(15)=225a+15b.$ So, we need to solve the equation $225a+15b=4\\,050$ for the parameter $b.$\n\nWe need to isolate the variable $b.$ To do this, we treat $a$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nFirst, we subtract $225a$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}225a+15b & =4\\,050 \\\\ 225a+15b-225a & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ 15b & =4\\,050-225a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $15:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15b & =4\\,050-225a \\\\ \\frac{15b}{15} & =\\frac{4\\,050-225a}{15} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{15}b}{\\cancel{15}} & =\\frac{4\\,050}{15}-\\frac{225a}{15} \\\\ b & =270-15a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $b=270-15a.$",
          "solution_evidence": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245623/observations/history-solution-q-167217-d5e87c262a2cb25115a7.html",
          "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245623/observations/history-q-167217-6e109da3aa88b99f3203.html"
